<title>USA: Seagull Energy completes offshore find.</title>
<headline>Seagull Energy completes offshore find.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seagull Energy Corp said Tuesday a Galveston Block 420 discovery yielded natural gas flows totaling 10.4 million cubic feet per day on tests of 52 cumulative feet of productive natural gas sands in four zones.</p>
<p>Seagull said it holds a 75 percent working interest in the well, which is located in the Gulf of Mexico about 30 miles south of Freeport, Texas, in 95 feet of water. The remaining interest is held by Barrett Resources Corp.</p>
<p>The partners are working to complete the necessary facilities so that production can be underway before the end of 1996, Seagull added.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
